const body = `<h1>Writing Classes: Quick Reference</h1>

<p>One page, no story, no lab. The shapes, signatures, and traps of the unit,
compressed. This is the page to keep open during builds and to re-read the
night before a test. Print it and mark it up.</p>

<h2>The Skeleton</h2>
<pre><code>public class Player {
    private String name;        // fields: always private
    private int hp;

    public Player(String name, int hp) {   // constructor
        this.name = name;                   // this. resolves shadowing
        this.hp = hp;
    }

    public String getName() { return name; }        // accessor
    public void setHp(int hp) { this.hp = hp; }     // mutator
    public String toString() { return name + " (" + hp + " hp)"; }
}</code></pre>

<h2>Encapsulation Rules</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Rule</th><th>Why</th></tr>
    <tr><td>fields private</td><td>outside code cannot corrupt state</td></tr>
    <tr><td>accessors public as needed</td><td>read access is a choice, not a default</td></tr>
    <tr><td>mutators validate</td><td>setHp(-5) must be rejected or clamped</td></tr>
    <tr><td>toString for printing</td><td>println(obj) calls it automatically</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>static vs instance</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr>
    <tr><td>belongs to class, no object needed</td><td>static (Math.abs, your Dice.roll)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>needs this object's data</td><td>instance (getName, length)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>called how</td><td>ClassName.method() vs obj.method()</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>this</h2>
<pre><code>this.name = name;   // field = parameter, when names collide
this(...);          // constructor calling another constructor (first line)</code></pre>

<h2>Scope</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Visible</th></tr>
    <tr><td>parameter</td><td>its method only</td></tr>
    <tr><td>local</td><td>from declaration to its block's closing brace</td></tr>
    <tr><td>field</td><td>everywhere in the class, this's lifetime</td></tr>
</table>



<h2>The Unit's Traps, One Line Each</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Forgetting this. in a shadowed assignment assigns the parameter to itself. The field stays null/0.</li>
    <li>No-arg constructor vanishes the moment you write any constructor. Provide it if you need it.</li>
    <li>Mutators without validation let hp go negative. Guard: if (hp &gt;= 0) this.hp = hp;</li>
    <li>toString must be exactly public String toString(). Any other signature is just a method.</li>
    <li>static method touching an instance field: does not compile. static knows no this.</li>
</ul>

<h2>See Also</h2>
<ul>
